\subsection{Solution Space and Constraint Boundaries}

Figure~\ref{fig:solution_space} maps the complete set of solutions
generated by the beam search across a $3 \times 3 \times 3$ grid
of objective weights $(w_1, w_2, w_3)$. Each point represents a
unique (launches, duration) outcome; diamond markers identify
Pareto-optimal solutions; the dashed step line traces the
empirical Pareto frontier. The red shaded band above the
horizontal constraint line ($T = T_{\max}$) marks the
infeasible region enforced by the maximum-period limit
(Eq.~\ref{eq:penalty}). The orange band below the
lead-time floor marks durations that cannot be achieved
regardless of weights because vehicle availability gates
(Eq.~\ref{eq:leadtime}) prevent earlier first launches.
Red stars indicate the tagged scenario{{ 's' if runs | length > 1 else '' }}.

